  "finding": "Open/short and MCU low/high-Z inhibit in ideal steady state. Reset/high-Z is default-deny through R36 and Q4-off, leaving CE pulled high from SYS. Firmware drives PB2 low before output mode and cannot request charge until 10ms after an accepted USB grant. A stuck-high MCU does not itself inhibit; operating temperature comparators still override it.",
  "required_resolution": [
    "Bench-capture SYS, V3V3, CHG_ALLOW, CHG_GUARD_GATE, CE and charge current during dead-pack USB insertion and removal; prove the real ramp preserves inhibit",
    "Qualify real NTC R-T envelope and mechanical thermal contact; electrically intact detached sensor is not detected",
    "Check MOS gate threshold, comparator sink/leakage, input common mode and supply tolerances over temperature",
    "Do not substitute a push-pull-output comparator directly: its outputs cannot be tied together in this topology"
  ],
  "not_proven": [
    "Physical startup/transient inhibit",
    "Cell-temperature threshold bounds",
    "16h runtime",
